{"step_index":117,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T11:23:35Z","thinking":"`attachments.redirect` functions as expected, successfully forwarding to a file retrieval operation. Confirmed that the target system correctly renders standard markdown images using the observed image embedding syntax. Now evaluating if a document identifier is necessary when referencing attachments within the target system, or if linking is handled implicitly.\n\n\nDocument creation will happen in the designated Outline location, within the \"Infra\" collection under \"3. Procédures & Runbooks.\" The attachment workflow must explicitly associate the image with the new document using `documentId`. The procedure will be composed in French, adhering to established wiki conventions.\n\nDecommissioning steps will include phases like \"Demande du dé-commissionnement\", \"Analyse d'impact et risques\", \"Validation CAB\", \"Mise à jour NetBox.\" The image will be incorporated into the French-language procedure document.\n\n\nConsidering the required sections for a comprehensive decommissioning procedure. The document will need a standardized header, clear objectives with defined scope, a visual workflow, and detailed step-by-step instructions. Each step will include actor responsibilities, prerequisites, actions, deliverables, and security considerations. Initial thoughts focus on a thorough breakdown of the 12 phases including supervision deactivation, technical shutdown, firewall rule removal, equipment removal, and reporting.\n\n\nThe decommissioning procedure's initial phase focuses on formalizing the request, ensuring all necessary details are captured, including hostname, IP addresses, functional role, equipment type, environment, reason for decommissioning, and the desired date. A crucial element involves identifying data owners and stakeholders.\n\nThe subsequent impact and risk analysis step requires a comprehensive inventory of dependencies across network configurations, web exposures, application integrations, data stores, and automation scripts. Risk assessment will define a quarantine window, and the Change Request (RFC) will detail the rollback plan.\n\nThe final element is the CAB (Change Advisory Board) review to validate the analysis's completeness.\n\n\nFollowing CAB approval, the operational phase begins with notifications to relevant teams. Next step requires updating a central inventory with the decommissioning status and associated metadata. Subsequently, supervision systems must be configured to prevent alerts and escalations. Finally, validate the backup and data retention plan, including full backups before shutdown.\n\n\nBackup configuration files and data to a secure storage location, adhering to the validated retention policy and verifying data integrity via checksums and read tests. Technical shutdown involves stopping services, OS shutdown, removing the server from automated inventories, and disabling SSH access, followed by a quarantine period. Security team will disable firewall rules associated with the equipment's IP, keeping the rules disabled during the quarantine period.\n\n\nFollowing the quarantine period, decommissioning involves definitive equipment removal: virtual machines are deleted, physical servers are dismantled and disks securely erased, and network/storage resources are cleaned up (SAN LUNs, NFS exports, virtual interfaces). DNS entries are removed and the central inventory system is updated, freeing the IP address.\n\nNext, firewall rules are permanently deleted, removing orphaned address objects, groups, and cleaning NAT tables and external publication rules. The final step is to create a technical decommissioning report.\n\n\nThe decommissioning report will include key information such as the decommissioning and definitive removal dates, backup references, and recovered disk/memory space. The Change Advisory Board (CAB) ticket will be closed with a \"Closed - Successful\" status, and the initiating ticket will be closed with final notification sent.\n\nA comprehensive operational checklist in an interactive table will be included, alongside a detailed rollback plan for issues identified during the quarantine period. A decommissioning report template will be developed. The ability to render markdown elements (tables, checkboxes, callout blocks, and code) within Outline documents must be verified.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport requests\n\nTOKEN = 'eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjY2ZDAwY2I0LWEzY2YtNDIyYS1hMjQ5LWVkMzA2NzEwZDdjZiIsImV4cGlyZXNBdCI6IjIwMjYtMTItMDhUMTA6NDU6MjcuNzkzWiIsInR5cGUiOiJzZXNzaW9uIiwic2VydmljZSI6ImF6dXJlIiwiaWF0IjoxNzg4ODY0MzI3fQ.tQTTmIeOP_H2i-10PROwjV-c_snixZFU5pG6CpKXXCk'\nBASE_URL = 'https://wiki.corp.intranet.local'\n\npayload = {\n    'title': 'Test Doc Verification',\n    'text': '# Test\\nThis is a test doc',\n    'collectionId': 'bda1a3da-cc3d-4c5d-92d1-d831dfbe2eae',\n    'parentDocumentId': 'fadb8718-bb7a-4349-b22f-4fdc83051340',\n    'publish': True\n}\n\nres = requests.post(f'{BASE_URL}/api/documents.create', headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {TOKEN}'}, json=payload, verify=False)\ndata = res.json()\nprint('Status:', res.status_code, 'OK:', data.get('ok'))\nif data.get('data'):\n    doc_id = data['data']['id']\n    print('Created doc id:', doc_id, 'url:', data['data']['url'])\n    # clean up immediately\n    del_res = requests.post(f'{BASE_URL}/api/documents.delete', headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {TOKEN}'}, json={'id': doc_id}, verify=False)\n    print('Cleaned up test doc:', del_res.json())\n\"","Cwd":"/home/koby","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing document creation with parent in Outline","toolSummary":"Test document creation with parent"}}]}
